CRIME NARRATIVE ARC — 18-BEAT STRUCTURE
No headings in script output
================================================================================

 1.  COLD OPEN MONTAGE — 4–7 non-chronological shock-lines pulled from later
     in the story (investigation / forensic pivot / confession / arrest /
     twist). No explanation, no resolution, no case name yet.
 2.  PIVOT LINE — one grounding "देखिए..." sentence that ends the montage and
     shifts tone into calm chronological narration.
 3.  Case label + stakes line
 4.  Story promise — "इस वीडियो में हम बताएंगे..."
 5.  VICTIM HUMANIZATION — who they were, what they loved, what they worked for
     [CRITICAL: before any crime detail appears]
 6.  Relationship setup — how victim and perpetrator were connected
 7.  THE SURFACE LIFE — how everything appeared normal from outside
 8.  THE CRACK — first sign something was wrong
 9.  THE HIDDEN WORLD — perpetrator's secret (affair / debt / plan)
10.  THE DECEPTION COVER — how the killer built their cover story
11.  OBJECT / FORENSIC HOOK appears — the one thing that breaks the lie
     [second biggest surprise — must land between minutes 4–8]
12.  INVESTIGATION BUILD — CDR / DNA / CCTV / postmortem / digital recovery
13.  KILLER AT PEAK — cover story working, public sympathizing, killer confident
14.  THE PIVOT — the one detail that collapses the cover story
15.  INTERROGATION CRACK — the exact moment the prepared story breaks
16.  CONFESSION / ARREST
17.  SYSTEMIC ANGLE — what institution / loophole made this possible
18.  VICTIM TRIBUTE — what was lost, not just the crime
19.  Reflection + comment question + Like/Subscribe CTA + धन्यवाद / जय हिंद

     NOTE: Every montage line from Beat 1 must be explicitly paid off at its
     proper chronological position in Beats 3–19 — this closes the loop the
     viewer's brain opened at the very start.

